 "subject": "How to find Finite Occupancy Estimate confidence intervals?",
 "messages_listed": 4,
 "last_activity": "2018-01-16T19:01:46Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "gFU1vzdeAwAJ",
   "from": "seanh...@trentu.ca",
   "author": "67eefb0e32c64fae",
   "date": "2018-01-15T21:49:11Z",
   "subject": "How to find Finite Occupancy Estimate confidence intervals?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello there! I am trying to find the finite occupancy estimate using code outlined in a few of the Unmarked examples, but I am unable to interpret the results. <div><br></div><div>Here is my code...  (fm1 is a null colext model):</div><div><br></div><div><div>&gt; re &lt;- ranef(fm1)</div><div>&gt; EBUP &lt;- bup(re, stat=&quot;mode&quot;)</div><div>&gt; CI &lt;- confint(re, level=0.95)</div><div>&gt; rbind(s_occup = c(Estimate = sum(EBUP), colSums(CI)))</div><div>        Estimate          </div><div>s_occup       13 5 21 4 21</div><div>&gt; rbind(PAO = c(Estimate = sum(EBUP), colSums(CI))/n)</div><div>     Estimate                        </div><div>PAO 0.6190476 0.2380952 1 0.1904762 1</div></div><div><br></div><div>I am guessing that the occupancy estimate is 0.6190476? But what are the confidence intervals?</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div><br></div><div>Sean</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mh4uMFNxAwAJ",
   "from": "seanh...@trentu.ca",
   "author": "67eefb0e32c64fae",
   "date": "2018-01-16T03:39:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to find Finite Occupancy Estimate confidence intervals?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Would also appreciate confirmation as to whether this is the correct way to estimate finite occupancy. I have already estimated infinite occupancy using:<div><br></div><div><div>fm1 &lt;- colext(psiformula = ~1, gammaformula = ~1, epsilonformula = ~1, pformula = ~1, data = FosnUMF, se = TRUE)</div><div>  backTransform(fm1,&quot;det&quot;) #Detection Estimate</div><div>  <b>backTransform(fm1,&quot;psi&quot;) #Infinite Occupancy Estimate</b></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "wxajC4UCAwAJ",
   "from": "Richard Chandler",
   "author": "403be63af7ebf220",
   "date": "2018-01-16T16:19:30Z",
   "subject": "Re: [unmarked] Re: How to find Finite Occupancy Estimate confidence intervals?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Hi Sean,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">You are correct that 0.619 is the estimate of the proportion of sites occupied in the sample. However, it’s a bit trickier to get the CIs because you need to condition on the observed data. One option is to simulate the latent occupancy state from the estimated posterior distributions. You can then compute summary statistics from these simulated values. For the occupancy case, you can simulate with a binomial distribution, like this:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">library(unmarked)\r\nexample(occu)\r\n\r\npmean &lt;- bup(re, stat=&quot;mean&quot;) # Posterior mean \r\n\r\nnSites &lt;- length(pmean)\r\nnSim &lt;- 1000\r\nz &lt;- matrix(NA, nSites, nSim)\r\nfor(i in 1:nSim) {\r\n    z[,i] &lt;- rbinom(nSites, 1, pmean) # Simulated occupancy states\r\n    }\r\nN &lt;- colSums(z) # number of sites occupied in each simulation\r\n\r\nquantile(N, c(0.025, 0.975))/nSites # 95% CI\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">I might add some functions to do this in a more general way for each model in unmarked. </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Richard</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">On Mon, Jan 15, 2018 at 10:39 PM,  &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">seanh...@trentu.ca</a>&gt; wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p></div></div>"
    ],
